B.a4s=s(['Arunachal Pradesh ("Land of the Dawn-lit Mountains") is the largest state by area among the Seven Sisters of Northeast India.',"Established as a full-fledged State on 20th February 1987 (24th State of the Indian Union via 55th Constitutional Amendment Act).","Capital & Largest City: Itanagar.","Area: 83,743 sq. km (14th largest state in India).","Population (2011 Census): 13,83,727 (Density: 17 persons/sq. km - lowest in India).","Literacy Rate: 65.38% (Male: 72.55%, Female: 57.70%).","Official Language: English.","High Court: Gauhati High Court (Permanent Itanagar Bench).","Legislature: Unicameral Legislative Assembly (60 seats).","Governor: Lt. Gen. Kaiwalya Trivikram Parnaik (Retd).","Chief Minister: Shri Pema Khandu."],t.s)
